# STAYS AT THE REPO ROOT even though the Dockerfiles live in docker/. Docker reads this from the BUILD
# CONTEXT, never from beside the Dockerfile, and both images build with the repo root as context (core
# copies from core/, the worker from worker/) — so one file covers both. Moving it into docker/ would not
# error; it would silently stop excluding anything, and node_modules would be sent to the daemon.
**/node_modules
**/.svelte-kit
**/build
**/dist
data
media
*.sqlite*
.git
docs/mocks/*.png
**/__pycache__
# `**/`, NOT a bare `.venv`: a root-anchored pattern misses `new-worker/.venv`, which is a MULTI-GB ML
# virtualenv — it would be uploaded to the daemon on every build and then ignored by the image.
**/.venv
# Durable DBOS state is per-box machine state. Copying a dev box's checkpoints into an image would make it
# try to recover another machine's in-flight workflows on first boot.
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
worker/wheelhouse/
*.whl
*.tar.gz
